.SH NAME
ivcap-artifact-create - Create a new artifact


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBivcap artifact create [flags] -n name -f file|-\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new artifact by uploading file content to IVCAP.

.PP
The MIME content-type is auto-detected from the file header when -t/--content-type
is omitted.  Detection uses the 'mimetype' library (500+ formats) with extension-based
overrides for ambiguous types (e.g. .tar.gz → application/x-compressed-tar).

.PP
When -t is provided it accepts either a full MIME type or a bare file extension:

.PP
-t application/x-compressed-tar   full MIME type
  -t tgz                            bare extension (same result)
  -t .tar.gz                        extension with dot (same result)

.PP
Supported extension shorthands include (but are not limited to):
  Archives:     tar, tgz/tar.gz, gz, bz2, xz, zst
  Earth/env:    nc/nc4, fits/fit/fts, hdf5/h5, zarr
  Bioinformat.: fasta/fa/fna/faa, fastq/fq, bam, sam, vcf, bcf, bed, gff, gff3, gtf
  Data science: parquet, arrow, mat, npy, npz

.PP
When reading from stdin (-f -) the first 512 bytes are sniffed and replayed into the
upload stream so no data is lost.  For piped tar.gz streams (where the extension is
unavailable) pass -t tgz or -t application/x-compressed-tar explicitly.

.PP
Files named *.zip, *.tar, *.tar.gz or *.tgz are indexed before upload and receive an RO-Crate 1.2
JSON-LD manifest aspect by default. Only the file name decides, so other ZIP-based formats such as
\&.docx are not indexed. Use --without-manifest to opt out. The manifest is a convenience: if an
archive cannot be indexed, or the aspect cannot be added, a warning is printed and the upload still
completes; run the same command again to retry the manifest. Content read from stdin is never
indexed.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--chunk-size\fP=10000000
	Chunk size in bytes for splitting large files: at least 65536, or -1 to upload without chunking

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--collection\fP=""
	Assigns artifact to a specific collection

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--content-type\fP=""
	Content type of artifact; auto-detected when omitted. Accepts a full MIME type (e.g. application/x-compressed-tar) or a bare extension (e.g. tgz, nc, fasta)

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	Path to file containing artifact content

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	Force creation of new artifact, even if already uploaded

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--license\fP="undefined"
	License of the content, recorded in the archive manifest: an SPDX identifier such as CC-BY-4.0 (not checked against the SPDX list), a license URL, or 'undefined'

.PP
\fB--manifest-schema\fP="urn:ivcap:schema:artifact.archive-manifest.1"
	Schema URN for the archive manifest aspect

.PP
\fB-n\fP, \fB--name\fP=""
	Human friendly name

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--policy\fP=""
	Policy controlling access

.PP
\fB--without-manifest\fP[=false]
	Do not add a file manifest for ZIP, TAR or TAR.GZ archives


